cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the methods paper (preferred) and
  the software itself when the specific implementation is relevant.
title: "lomad: Local Moving Average Decoupling"
abstract: >-
  Detects localized periods of decoupling between two time series using
  correlations between local moving averages. Trends are extracted by moving
  average, noise autocovariance is estimated from the residual variogram, and
  the local sample correlation is compared against its shared-trend benchmark
  by pointwise one-sided Z-tests with a Benjamini-Yekutieli step-up correction
  controlling the false discovery rate under arbitrary dependence. Ships a
  quality-controlled snippet of dissolved oxygen and pH monitoring data from
  the Morro Bay estuary, collected by the Central and Northern California Ocean
  Observing System (CeNCOOS) and contributed by Emily Bockmon.
